++# Meta Agent Improvements
++
++## Changes made this generation:
++
++### 1. task_agent.py prompt improvements
++- Added **absolute requirement** that the Task Agent must make a structural change to the core search mechanism, not just tweak parameters. Explicitly lists failure modes (changing F, CR, swarm_size, adding tiny perturbations) as unacceptable.
++- Added a **concrete SHADE implementation guide** with step-by-step pseudocode for success-history memory, current-to-pbest mutation, archive, and Lehmer mean updates.
++- Added a **vectorized NumPy mutation/crossover template** for SHADE/JADE, with explicit code showing how to sample F/CR per-individual, do pbest mutation, and binomial crossover using NumPy array operations instead of per-individual Python loops.
++- Added a **performance/timeout warning** section explaining that a timeout scores zero. Documented the concrete gen_11 failure where an L-SHADE implementation with nested Python for-loops timed out (>120s on a 20D sphere with 2000 evals).
++- Made the smoke test **mandatory** before finishing, with a concrete Python script to run.
++- Emphasized that FAST CODE IS AS IMPORTANT AS CORRECT CODE.
++
++### 2. hyper_agent.py prompt improvements
++- Added mandatory step-by-step actions for the Meta Agent: find the latest generation, read the diff, read chat history, and react to parameter-only tweaks or evaluation failures.
++- Added a requirement to write a summary of changes to `/hada/agent_output/hyper_agent_improvements.md`.
++
++## Rationale
++- Prior generations plateaued because Task Agents only tweaked PSO/DE parameter values instead of replacing the algorithm.
++- When Task Agents finally attempted structural changes (L-SHADE), the first implementation was too slow (nested Python loops) and timed out, scoring zero.
++- These prompt changes should push future Task Agents to: (1) actually replace the search algorithm, and (2) do so with vectorized NumPy code that runs fast enough to pass the evaluation timeout.
